; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Category assignment for Banyu Langit symbols.
;
; This file is NOT a quote format. It is imported with its own category CSVs
; (categories_us.csv, categories_idx.csv) and only assigns metadata to symbols
; that already exist.
;
; WHY $AUTOADD 0:
;   With $AUTOADD 1 a typo in a ticker would CREATE an empty symbol, and the
;   database would grow phantom rows that hold no quotes and silently inflate
;   the symbol count that other gates rely on. The categories are written from
;   the same KEPT set as the quotes, so every ticker here already exists.
;
; WHY $OVERWRITE 1:
;   Without it, MARKET/GROUP/INDUSTRY/SECTORNAME are only applied to NEW
;   symbols. Re-running the nightly category import would then change nothing
;   once the symbol existed, and a corrected sector would never land.
;
; WHY $NOQUOTES 1:
;   Tells the importer these rows carry no OHLC. Without it every category row
;   is also parsed as a quote and rejected, which trips $BREAKONERR.
;
; WHY $BREAKONERR 1 and no $DEBUG:
;   A silently skipped line here puts a stock in the wrong market, which is the
;   same class of error as a bar that never imported - but harder to notice,
;   because the chart still works. Fail the whole file instead. $DEBUG stays
;   off so no import.log is written for a metadata pass; the VBScript gate
;   verifies by counting symbols per market afterwards.
;
; Import order: quotes FIRST, categories SECOND. The reverse order assigns
; nothing because $AUTOADD 0 requires the symbol to exist already.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

$FORMAT Ticker,Market,Group,SectorName,IndustryName
$SEPARATOR ,
$NOQUOTES 1
$AUTOADD 0
$OVERWRITE 1
$BREAKONERR 1
$CONT 1
